winebus: SQUARK_FAKEPAD=<path> adds a virtual SDL gamepad driven through a FIFO.

For testing input without a controller at hand, and for driving a program with gamepad input in the
background. winebus attaches an SDL virtual joystick of the game controller type, 045e:02fd and named
"squark fakepad", like a Bluetooth Xbox Wireless Controller, and reads text lines from the FIFO at
<path> (made if missing): "<axis> <value>" with lx, ly, rx, ry, lt, rt in raw SDL values (-32768 to
32767; sticks negative up and left, as SDL reports them, triggers -32768 released and 32767 fully
pressed), "<button> <0|1>" with a, b, x, y, back, guide, start, ls, rs, lb, rb, up, down, left, right,
or "reset". Lines end in a newline or ';'. The pad goes through SDL's game controller API and the
rest of winebus like a real one, so XInput, DirectInput and Windows.Gaming.Input see it as they
would a real pad. Needs the SDL bus.

Unset or empty: no change.

